runs.developer_explanation:
The encode() method calls C_METHODS.get(httpMethod) even when httpMethod might be null (if the request method string is missing). EnumMap does not allow null keys and will throw a NullPointerException. Add a null check before calling get(), for example:
```
HttpMethod httpMethod = method == null ? null : HttpMethod.fromString(method);
HttpField methodField = httpMethod != null ? C_METHODS.get(httpMethod) : null;
```
This prevents the exception and correctly handles legacy or malformed requests.
